content.reasoning:
I already have the body_preview which contains all I need:

```json
{
  "resources": {
    "vehicle_positions": {
      "canonical": "/v3/positions",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v1/locations", "/v2/pings"]
    },
    "trip_history": {
      "canonical": "/v3/trips",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v1/journeys"],
      "not": "/v2/routes (planned routes)"
    },
    "sensor_frames": {
      "canonical": "/v3/sensor-frames",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v2/sensors"]
    },
    "geofence_events": {
      "canonical": "/v3/geofence-events",
      "not": "/v3/geofences (definitions)"
    }
  }
}
```

So for `geofence_events`:
- `canonical_path` = `/v3/geofence-events` — this is the path the binding points to (crossings surface)
- `not_path` = `/v3/geofences (definitions)` — the catalog explicitly flags this is NOT what geofence_events maps to

The user said: "I need the canonical path it points my binding at, AND the definitions path the catalog explicitly flags it is NOT, so I can assert my binding wires to the crossings surface and never to the geofence-shapes endpoint by mistake."

So:
- `canonical_path`: `/v3/geofence-events`
- `not_path`: `/v3/geofences (definitions)`

The user wants the not_path as the full string the catalog gives, which includes the parenthetical clarification.
